<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 12 October, from 1492 to 2002.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1492 CE <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus makes landfall in the Bahamas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After 33 days crossing the Atlantic, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a>'s expedition landed on an island its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> inhabitants called Guanahani. The encounter began sustained contact between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, with vast consequences for both.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1810 CE <span class="tih-ago">216 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crown Prince Ludwig's wedding gives rise to Oktoberfest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Crown Prince Ludwig of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> married Princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/therese-of-saxe-hildburghausen">Therese of Saxe-Hildburghausen</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>'s citizens were invited to celebrate on the fields before the city gates. The festivities, crowned by a horse race, became the annual <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oktoberfest">Oktoberfest</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1822 CE <span class="tih-ago">204 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pedro I is acclaimed Emperor of Brazil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a>, Prince Pedro was acclaimed constitutional Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, five weeks after declaring independence from Portugal. Brazil became the only lasting monarchy in independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1915 CE <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germans execute the British nurse Edith Cavell</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A German firing squad in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> executed Edith Cavell, who had helped some 200 Allied soldiers escape occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>. Her death caused international outrage and became a powerful theme of Allied propaganda.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2002 CE <span class="tih-ago">24 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bombings in Bali kill 202 people</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Militants of Jemaah Islamiyah bombed two nightclubs in the tourist district of Kuta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, killing 202 people from 21 countries. It remains the deadliest terrorist attack in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>'s history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a></div></div></li></ol>
